ng the last term, we get\n\n$$\n(x-1{)}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-1$ and $q=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/title "Completing the Square on a Quadratic Expression with a Negative Linear Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d53fe67-7a37-5135-9bda-59dc26da7eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5,\\text{ }q=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400939} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5c7488-0854-5209-9e72-78867a6a1be6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=5,\\text{ }q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400940} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ec775e-a603-50a4-a821-b02cc8bdf4a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-10,\\text{ }q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400941} {:answer/id #uuid "91f01cc1-7dda-5a0a-a09b-a1edcdb5224f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5,\\text{ }q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400942} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e81c67-49e3-5deb-9f3d-4bfdd5f4f433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=5,\\text{ }q=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91f01cc1-7dda-5a0a-a09b-a1edcdb5224f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p=-5,\\text{ }q=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400942} :answer-field/id #uuid "c559c184-d951-52c2-ae9b-1fd6b5cd4853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a81398bc-73ed-504a-b8b3-ef512650d7f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-141622" :question/problem "If the expression ${y}^{2}-10y+30$ is written as $(y+p{)}^{2}+q,$ then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n